# Deny everything, then allow only what the Dockerfile actually COPYs.
#
# Deliberately an allowlist. The context otherwise included montrek/uploads
# (customer files) and db_backups (SQL dumps) -- 18GB shipped to the daemon on
# every build, and one `COPY . .` away from being baked into an image that gets
# pushed to a registry.
#
# If you add a COPY/ADD to the Dockerfile, add a matching `!` line here or the
# build will fail with "file not found".
*

!bin/entrypoints/montrek-entrypoint.sh
